  "summary_en": "China's State Council Order No. 761 promulgating the Interim Regulations on unmanned aircraft flight management, effective 1 January 2024. It classifies drones by weight, sets airspace, flight approval, airworthiness, operator licensing, real-name registration and insurance rules, and prescribes penalties.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Drones classified as micro, light, small, medium and large by weight and performance.",
   "Medium and large civil drones require airworthiness approval; operators need licences and certificates.",
   "Flight plans need air traffic authority approval, with controlled airspace rules.",
   "Real-name registration, unique product identification codes and liability insurance required.",
   "Graded fines, suspensions and licence revocation for violations; effective 1 January 2024."
